you  in the first two parts of our three-part  series we explored the procedures in  place for first contact and the possible  stances intelligent beings could take on  humanity in this final installment we're  going to take a look at the potential  social legal and theological  ramifications of alien arrival before we  start looking at the possibilities let's  establish our baseline these  hypothetical scenarios only work if the  aliens we encounter are at least  somewhat similar to humans in terms of  biology and intellect with such a vast  universe out there who knows what form  intelligent life could take for the sake  of this video we're going to assume that  the aliens we encounter are roughly  similar to humans in all the necessary  ways to allow communication between our  species in today's world it seems we've  seen new acts of violence hatred and  xenophobia everyday humans as a species  have a history of disagreement war  subjugation and distrust what if we  added extraterrestrial beings to the mix  would all of our differences suddenly  seem inconsequential  how would you manatee respond to so  radically change aliens living side by  side with humans has long been explored  in science fiction everything from star  trek to district 9 to call each having  their own interpretation of how well the  different species would get along when  district 9 was released back in 2009 it  sparked some interesting conversation  what if aliens arrived and they're not  here to destroy us or to help us what if  they're simply refugees and need a place  to stay for a while in the film aliens  were forced to live in slums and anti  alien sentiment was prevalent many  people considered this creative choice  to be a commentary on contemporary race  relations especially considering the  clear parallel to apartheid South Africa  apartheid was a very dark period in  South African history officially lasting  from 1948 to 1991 it was a system of  institutionalized racial segregation  under apartheid housing and employment  opportunities were dictated by race put  simply black suffered worse and worse  discrimination over the years often  being subjected to social exclusion  forced relocation and violence at the  hands of the white ruling class  officially that's all behind us but it's  clear that even today these social  problems still exist whether we like to  admit it or not humans tend to group  together with people like themselves and  ostracize those who are different that  doesn't bode well for any  extraterrestrials who decide to stop by  of course  alien rival could also be a good thing a  giant tentacled monster landing on earth  could help humans realize that we're all  one species after all and perhaps our  differences aren't as vast as we think  what about the legal ramifications say  an alien lands on the White House lawn  as aliens often do he obviously has no  passport or citizenship anywhere on  earth so what do we do with him  initially such visitors may only have  the protection of animal cruelty  statutes as they're not human and  therefore have no human rights however  if the alien were sufficiently humanoid  in appearance it's no stretch of the  imagination that the governments of the  world would be more willing to classify  them as something for lack of a better  term more significant than animals but  where would that distinction put our  alien friend what rights would it afford  him probably not many if we learned  anything from history not even a hundred  years ago women couldn't vote in the  United States of course it's clearly a  very different situation one problem  that our alien friend might have  particular trouble with especially if he  arrives within the next four to eight  years is that he would technically be an  illegal immigrant unfortunately for him  there's really no way around that  he can't exactly go through the proper  immigration process without physically  being on earth hopefully the president  would make an exception to his current  stance on immigrants and refugees  otherwise children decades from now will  read in their history books how we  deported the first alien ever to visit  planet Earth perhaps the most  interesting effect of alien arrival  would be its impact on world religions  while religious beliefs vary widely  around the world most holy books would  require a thorough reinterpretation to  come to terms with the existence of  other intelligent beings the United  States would likely face the biggest  religious crisis because of its high  population of evangelical Christians  along with several other fundamentalist  branches extraterrestrial life would be  especially problematic for Christianity  because of its geocentric nature many  practicing Christians hold the opinion  that the earth is unique and special to  God and indeed earth is so far the  planet best suited to life as we know it  but if aliens were to make themselves  own it would likely cause a crisis of  faith in many conservative Christians  however in one survey of people with  many different religious beliefs people  indicated that their faith would not be  affected by the discovery of  extraterrestrial intelligence such  surveys tend to show that only a small  percentage of the religious population  would consider their beliefs  fundamentally contradicted by alien life  perhaps the closest comparison one can  currently make is to the advent of the  theory of evolution as many believe the  biblical creation story is directly  contradicted by the process of evolution  there's been a fundamentalist backlash  against it on the other hand we've also  seen many religious people accept the  fact that evolution is undeniable and  integrate that into their belief system  this theological flexibility will  definitely be required in the case of  intelligent alien life two more  possibilities are that our alien  neighbors may dismiss the religions  earth instead providing us a natural  explanation for everything or eliminate  religion as we understand it and  introduce humanity to an  all-encompassing face of course this is  all speculation  who knows how we would interact with  extraterrestrial intelligence even if  they do share similar physiology and  communication methods it would be such a  monumental change that everything we  know about social progress and legal  procedure could be thrown out the window  alien arrival would require a massive  overhaul of national and international  law social accommodations and religious  interpretation as for what society would  look like after this metamorphosis is  complete who can say we'll just have to  wait to find out be sure to check out  the links in the description if you'd  like to read more about the topics  covered in this video  come join the second thought family on  discord follow the link in the  description to find a great place to  chat with other subscribers contributors  and me if you enjoyed this video please  take a moment to subscribe to my channel  your support really does make a big  difference feel free to leave a like or  a dislike as you please and leave a  comment down below with how you think  society would change with alien arrival  you can watch parts 1 &amp; 2 of this video  by clicking here or binge watch all of  my videos by clicking here thanks for  watching and I'll see you in the next  video  you  [Music]

